WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.980
In the UK in 2023, fewer than one
worker in a hundred worked in farming:

2
00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.030
0.9 per cent.

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.870
In Ethiopia, the same
year, it was 62.2 per cent.

4
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.910
India sits in between, at 43.5 per cent.

5
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.030
And the shares move.

6
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:24.650
In 1991, 77.2 per cent of
Ethiopia's workers farmed.

7
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.850
So why do so few people farm in Britain,
while most Ethiopian workers do?

8
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.910
Is Britain just too cold?

9
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.170
In this mission, you'll
sort jobs into four sectors,

10
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.750
from mining and farming to research.

11
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.530
Then you'll track how each
country's jobs have changed,

12
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.250
and test a model of that change.

13
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.470
Your mission: explain why
so few UK workers farm,

14
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.630
while most Ethiopian workers do.
